{
  "title": "CHAPTER 10: TAX STRUCTURE IN INDIA",
  "order": 8,
  "blocks": [
    {
      "id": "hea8eq5",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "1. MEANING AND OBJECTIVES OF TAXATION"
    },
    {
      "type": "keyFacts",
      "title": "Key Takeaways",
      "items": [
        "Taxation is a compulsory contribution without guaranteed direct benefits to the taxpayer.",
        "Adam Smith outlined four canons of taxation: Equality, Certainty, Convenience, and Economy.",
        "GST is a destination-based indirect tax introduced on 1 July 2017, replacing VAT and Service Tax.",
        "CBDT administers direct taxes while CBIC oversees indirect taxes in India.",
        "The GST Council operates under Article 279A where the Centre holds 1/3 vote weight and States hold 2/3.",
        "Tax Buoyancy greater than 1 indicates tax revenue grows faster than GDP."
      ],
      "id": "ie7kif5"
    },
    {
      "type": "statStrip",
      "stats": [
        {
          "label": "GST Implementation",
          "value": "1 July 2017",
          "icon": "calendar"
        },
        {
          "label": "GST Council Article",
          "value": "Article 279A",
          "icon": "book"
        },
        {
          "label": "Centre Vote Weight",
          "value": "1/3",
          "icon": "info"
        },
        {
          "label": "Council Decision Majority",
          "value": "3/4th",
          "icon": "check"
        }
