      "id": "2zilbiv"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "Tax is a compulsory contribution imposed by the government on individuals and businesses to raise revenue for public expenditure. It is not a voluntary payment and no direct benefit is guaranteed to the taxpayer.",
      "id": "zwtc6md"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "Objectives of Taxation:<br/>• Raise revenue for government expenditure<br/>• Reduce income inequality<br/>• Control inflation<br/>• Promote economic growth<br/>• Discourage harmful consumption (sin goods)<br/>",
      "id": "hn5k0ni"
    },
    {
      "id": "a9jlqcy",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "2. CANONS OF TAXATION (ADAM SMITH)"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "• Canon of Equality – Tax should be based on ability to pay.<br/>• Canon of Certainty – Tax amount and time should be clear.<br/>• Canon of Convenience – Tax should be easy to pay.<br/>• Canon of Economy – Cost of collection should be low.<br/>",
      "id": "qxlxta9"
    },
    {
      "id": "pcbw150",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "3. CLASSIFICATION OF TAXES"
