      "level": 2,
      "content": "8. TYPES OF TAX RATES"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "Progressive Tax – Rate increases with income.<br/>Regressive Tax – Rate decreases as income rises.<br/>Proportional Tax – Same rate for all income levels.<br/>",
      "id": "6s37rnj"
    },
    {
      "id": "mas1z92",
      "type": "table",
      "rows": [
        {
          "isHeader": true,
          "cells": [
            "<p><strong>Type</strong></p>",
            "<p><strong>Meaning</strong></p>"
          ]
        },
        {
          "isHeader": false,
          "cells": [
            "<p>Progressive</p>",
            "<p>Rate increases with income</p>"
          ]
        },
        {
          "isHeader": false,
          "cells": [
            "<p>Regressive</p>",
            "<p>Rate decreases as income rises</p>"
          ]
        },
        {
          "isHeader": false,
          "cells": [
            "<p>Proportional</p>",
            "<p>Same rate for all incomes</p>"
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "f4w118w",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "9. TAX ADMINISTRATION IN INDIA"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "• CBDT – Direct taxes administration.<br/>• CBIC – Indirect taxes administration.<br/>• GST Council – Decides GST rates and structure.<br/>",
      "id": "6w7prwo"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "<strong>10. TAX-TO-GDP RATIO &amp; TAX BUOYANCY</strong>",
      "id": "bar2rpk"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "Tax-to-GDP Ratio measures tax revenue as percentage of GDP.<br/>Higher ratio indicates better revenue mobilisation.<br/><br/>Tax Buoyancy measures responsiveness of tax revenue to changes in GDP.",
      "id": "v1eqp40"
    },
    {
      "type": "comparisonTable",
      "headers": [
        "Tax Structure",
        "Rate Variation",
        "Key Characteristic"
      ],
      "rows": [
        [
          "Progressive Tax",
          "Rate increases with income",
          "Promotes equity; higher income pays higher percentage"
        ],
        [
          "Regressive Tax",
          "Rate decreases as income rises",
          "Higher relative burden on lower-income individuals"
        ],
        [
          "Proportional Tax",
          "Same rate for all income levels",
          "Flat percentage tax applied uniformly across all income"
        ]
      ],
      "id": "ho5cezk"
    },
